title: "WMT24++ human post-edited references"
info: "This document contains English news articles from multiple outlets covering arts and culture, urban planning, gender equality, labor strikes, EU packaging regulations, and U.S. environmental enforcement. The content appears in news publications and is aimed at general readers. Translators should be aware that the document is a mixed collection of unrelated news segments, each with its own register and terminology, and should treat each group independently."
standard: "Use Simplified Chinese (zh-CN) with standard Mandarin punctuation and spacing conventions. Proper names of people, organizations, and places should follow established Chinese translations where they exist; otherwise, transliterate according to standard practice and retain the original in parentheses on first occurrence. Keep product names, legal document titles, and organization names untranslated where no official Chinese equivalent exists. Maintain a neutral, journalistic register appropriate for news reporting. Do not translate quoted speech into a different register than the surrounding text. Dates, numbers, and currency should follow Chinese conventions."

[news]
