<test-en-news-brisbanetimes-com-au-228963-6>
source: "Adapt the old, accommodate the new to solve issue"
target: "改造旧居所，容纳新移民，解决居住问题"
type: sentence
emotion: [neutral, serious]
status: final
context: "Headline of an opinion piece on urban planning and housing, arguing for adapting old buildings and accommodating new development. The reader is a general news audience; the headline should be concise and persuasive. Preceding segment: The Tierra del Sol Gallery is located at 7414 Santa Monica Blvd. For information, visit t… Following segment: At the precinct level, we just need to look at the Sydney CBD as an example of an area wh…"

<test-en-news-brisbanetimes-com-au-228963-7>
source: "At the precinct level, we just need to look at the Sydney CBD as an example of an area which has grown from its pre-settlement landscape into a two-storey city, from a maximum height of 150 feet to the soaring towers of today. At a much scaled-down level, the same can occur across Sydney's town centres located around transport nodes. Inner suburbs must also evolve, with a swing to more affordable apartment living at heights below the tree tops on key sites. Of course, the new growth in housing needs to be well-designed and trees, landscaping and parks need to be included along with other essential infrastructure."
target: "在区域层面，我们只需要以悉尼中央商务区为例。这个地区一路走来，从原生地貌到两层民居，再从最高不过150英尺的建筑，到如今高耸入云的摩天楼。在更小的尺度上，交通枢纽周边的悉尼市区各中心也可能遵循同样的发展路径。近郊也必须发展起来，在关键地段建设低于树顶高度、更经济适用的公寓楼。当然，新开发的住房需要精心设计，综合考量树木、景观、公园以及其他必要的基础设施。"
type: description
emotion: [neutral, objective]
status: final
context: "Paragraph from an urban planning opinion article discussing how Sydney's CBD grew over time and how similar growth could occur in town centres and inner suburbs. The tone is analytical and persuasive, aimed at general readers. Preceding segment: Adapt the old, accommodate the new to solve issue Following segment: Our planning system also needs to adapt so that planners in suburban councils, who seem t…"

<test-en-news-brisbanetimes-com-au-228963-8>
source: "Our planning system also needs to adapt so that planners in suburban councils, who seem to be less supportive of change, are not the only determinants of the future shape of their suburbs. A way forward could be to have an independent decision-making body that championed quality design as long as it fitted below the tree tops and incorporated family living, large balconies, common gardens and presented a friendly appearance. This could be a role for the current NSW government architect working within a carefully crafted complying code."
target: "我们的规划体系也需要调整，使郊区市政委员会的规划者（他们似乎不太支持变革）不再一手把持郊区未来形态的话语权。未来的方向可能是建立独立的决策机构来大力倡导优质设计：高度在树顶以下，融入家庭生活设施、大阳台、公共花园和友好外观。这也许是目前新南威尔士州政府的建筑专家在精心制定的合规规范中能够发挥的作用。"
type: description
emotion: [neutral, serious]
status: final
context: "Paragraph from an urban planning opinion article proposing an independent body to oversee suburban development and design quality. The tone is argumentative and policy-oriented. Preceding segment: At the precinct level, we just need to look at the Sydney CBD as an example of an area wh… Following segment: Over the past decade, our lives have changed through technology, with many working from h…"

<test-en-news-brisbanetimes-com-au-228963-9>
source: "Over the past decade, our lives have changed through technology, with many working from home, and Sydney has gained an impressive network of metro and light rail systems. Our ability to purchase online has changed the way we shop, and friends and family seem closer because of smartphone communication. All of these adaptations from one system to another can also occur in our built environment through a planning focus on adaptive reuse rather than preferencing heritage preservation."
target: "在过去的十年里，科技改变了我们的生活，许多人开始在家工作，悉尼也建成了令人印象深刻的地铁和轻轨网络。网购改变了我们的购物方式，智能手机的普及也拉近了朋友和家人之间的距离。同样地，如果城市规划的重点放在建筑的活化再利用上，而不是一味优先考虑老建筑保护，我们业已成型的环境也可以实现这样的转变和适应，实现系统层面的变革。"
type: description
emotion: [neutral, objective]
status: final
context: "Paragraph from an urban planning opinion article drawing parallels between technological adaptation in daily life and the need for adaptive reuse in the built environment. The tone is reflective and persuasive. Preceding segment: Our planning system also needs to adapt so that planners in suburban councils, who seem t… Following segment: Chris Johnson is a former NSW government architect (1995-2005) and executive director, NS…"

<test-en-news-brisbanetimes-com-au-228963-10>
source: "Chris Johnson is a former NSW government architect (1995-2005) and executive director, NSW Department of Planning (2005-2009). He was CEO of Urban Taskforce Australia between 2011 and 2019."
target: "克里斯·约翰逊曾任新南威尔士州政府建筑专家（1995-2005 年）和新南威尔士州规划部执行主任（2005-2009 年）。2011 年至 2019 年，他曾担任澳大利亚城市特别工作组的首席执行官。"
type: description
emotion: [neutral, formal]
status: final
