<test-en-news-csmonitor-com-7750-12>
source: "Last year, the World Economic Forum forecast that it would take five generations to achieve gender equality in every nation. Now the World Bank wants to rapidly accelerate that time frame."
target: "去年，世界经济论坛预测，全球实现性别平等需要五代人的时间。现在，世界银行希望迅速加快这一进程。"
type: sentence
emotion: [neutral, objective]
status: final
context: "Opening sentence of a news article on gender equality, citing forecasts from the World Economic Forum and the World Bank's intention to speed up progress. The tone is factual and journalistic. Preceding segment: A final push for female equality Following segment: The international financial institution is poised to launch a strategy aimed at significa…"

<test-en-news-csmonitor-com-7750-13>
source: "The international financial institution is poised to launch a strategy aimed at significantly advancing the rights and economic opportunities for girls and women by 2030. The plan focuses on improving inclusivity and resilience through access to finance, technological innovation, and changes in public policy and law."
target: "这家国际金融机构准备推出一项战略，旨在到 2030 年大幅提升女童和妇女的权利和经济机会。该计划的重点是通过资金支持、技术创新以及公共政策和法律变革，提高包容性和韧性。"
type: sentence
emotion: [neutral, objective]
status: final
context: "Opening paragraph of a news article about a major international financial institution's gender equality strategy. The reader is a general news audience; the tone is factual and forward-looking. Preceding segment: Last year, the World Economic Forum forecast that it would take five generations to achie… Following segment: \"Recent research demonstrates that both social norms and mindsets can change, for example…"

<test-en-news-csmonitor-com-7750-14>
source: "\"Recent research demonstrates that both social norms and mindsets can change, for example, that engaging men and boys can foster their support and buy-in for gender equality,\" a consultative draft of the plan states. \"Positive gender outcomes can be accelerated and scaled with a better understanding of ... how social norms and mindsets shape everyday expectations, priorities, and practices.\""
target: "“最近的研究表明，社会规范和思维方式都可以改变，例如，让成年和未成年的男性参与进来，可以培养他们对性别平等的支持和认同，”该计划的一份咨询草案指出，“如果能更好地了解社会规范和思维方式如何塑造日常期望、优先事项和行为方式，就能加快实现和扩大积极的性别平等成果。”"
type: sentence
emotion: [formal, objective]
status: final
context: "Direct quotation from a consultative draft of the institution's plan, cited within a news article. The quoted material is formal institutional language, and the translator should preserve that register. Preceding segment: The international financial institution is poised to launch a strategy aimed at significa… Following segment: Shifts in thought are harder to quantify than bank loans for rural women or school enroll…"

<test-en-news-csmonitor-com-7750-15>
source: "Shifts in thought are harder to quantify than bank loans for rural women or school enrollment for girls. Yet there is plenty of evidence that female agency can move mountains. In Iran, for example, women have led the greatest threat to the Islamic government in 40 years simply by refusing to comply with laws that force them to cover their hair. In some of the 130 countries with minimum quotas for female representation in government, such as India, male resistance to female voting and political activism has eased."
target: "与向农村妇女提供银行贷款或提高女童入学率相比，思维方式的转变更难量化。但有大量证据表明，女性的力量可以移山倒海。例如，在伊朗，女性仅仅因为拒绝遵守强制她们佩戴头巾的法律，就对伊斯兰政府构成了 40 年来最大的威胁。在全球范围内，在印度等 130 个对女性在政府机构中的人数设定了下限的国家，男性对女性投票和参政的阻力有所减弱。"
type: sentence
emotion: [objective, serious]
status: final
context: "Analytical passage in a news article arguing that shifts in social attitudes can be as significant as measurable economic outcomes. The writer uses a vivid idiom about female agency and cites Iran and India as examples. Preceding segment: \"Recent research demonstrates that both social norms and mindsets can change, for example… Following segment: In some rural African communities, civil society organizations are replacing a harmful ri…"

<test-en-news-csmonitor-com-7750-16>
source: "In some rural African communities, civil society organizations are replacing a harmful rite of passage with health education. One such program helped Kamanda Timayio, leader of the Masai village of Maparasha, Kenya, change his mind about female genital mutilation. He told Le Monde that he had \"emerged from ignorance\" and would abandon the practice."
target: "在一些非洲农村社区，民间社会组织正在用健康教育取代有害的成年礼。其中一个项目帮助肯尼亚马帕拉沙马赛村的村长卡曼达·蒂马约改变了对女性割礼的看法。他告诉《世界报》，他已经“摆脱了愚昧”，并将放弃这种做法。"
type: sentence
emotion: [neutral, serious]
status: final
context: "News article passage describing a specific program in rural Kenya that persuaded a Masai village leader to abandon female genital mutilation. Includes a direct quote from the leader as reported by Le Monde. Preceding segment: Shifts in thought are harder to quantify than bank loans for rural women or school enroll… Following segment: The World Bank cites other examples. From 1970 to 2022, Bangladesh quadrupled female lite…"

<test-en-news-csmonitor-com-7750-17>
source: "The World Bank cites other examples. From 1970 to 2022, Bangladesh quadrupled female literacy rates and doubled female participation in the labor force. Its gross domestic product more than tripled. The change gathered its own momentum. Recruiting salaried women as teachers and health workers from within their own communities boosted trust \"and made women's mobility and work more socially acceptable.\""
target: "世界银行还列举了其他例子。从 1970 年到 2022 年，孟加拉国女性识字率翻了两番，女性劳动力参与率翻了一番。其国内生产总值增长了两倍多。这种变化积聚了动力。从社区内部招募女性担任有薪教师和卫生工作者的做法增强了信任，“并使女性的流动和工作在社会上更容易被接受。”"
type: sentence
emotion: [objective, neutral]
status: final
context: "News article passage citing World Bank statistics on Bangladesh's progress in female literacy and labor participation. The tone is factual and explanatory, with a short quoted phrase at the end. Preceding segment: In some rural African communities, civil society organizations are replacing a harmful ri… Following segment: The bank's plan would target norms and institutions that may still require generational s…"

<test-en-news-csmonitor-com-7750-18>
source: "The bank's plan would target norms and institutions that may still require generational shifts. It has taken Rwanda more than two decades to establish itself as a model for land reforms that boost economic empowerment for women.\"No one benefits if women are held back,\" Rwanda President Paul Kagame said, arguing for land reform in 2015. \"We have to change mindsets, not just the laws.\""
target: "世界银行的计划将针对那些可能仍需几代人才能转变的规范和制度。卢旺达花了 20 多年时间推进增强女性经济权能的土地改革，最终成为典范。“如果女性受到阻碍，没有人会受益，”卢旺达总统保罗·卡加梅在 2015 年主张土地改革时表示，“我们必须改变观念，而不仅仅是法律。”"
type: sentence
emotion: [serious, objective]
status: final
context: "News article passage about the World Bank's long-term goals for changing social norms, using Rwanda's land reform as an example. Includes a direct quote from Rwanda's president urging changes in mindset. Preceding segment: The World Bank cites other examples. From 1970 to 2022, Bangladesh quadrupled female lite… Following segment: The World Bank hopes to spread that message."

<test-en-news-csmonitor-com-7750-19>
