<test-en-news-economist-14223-20>
source: "German farmers and train drivers are scaring Germany's bosses"
target: "德国农民和火车司机让老板们心惊肉跳"
type: sentence
emotion: [urgent, serious]
status: final
context: "Headline of a news article about labor unrest in Germany. It is designed to grab the reader's attention and uses a slightly dramatic tone. Preceding segment: The World Bank hopes to spread that message. Following segment: In Germany, where workers and bosses run many companies jointly, a big strike is unusual.…"

<test-en-news-economist-14223-21>
source: "In Germany, where workers and bosses run many companies jointly, a big strike is unusual. A wave of big strikes is almost unheard of. Right now the country of \"co-determination\" is simultaneously facing an eight-day \"action week\" by irate farmers, who blocked roads with tractors, a three-day strike of railway workers and, to top it off, a looming strike of doctors, who already closed surgeries between Christmas and New Year's Day. This Mistgabelmop (pitchfork mob), as some have taken to calling it, will test Germany's harmonious labour relations in the year to come."
target: "在德国，许多公司都由工人和老板共同经营，大规模罢工并不常见。多行业大规模罢工潮更是闻所未闻。现在，这个“共同决策”的国家正面临着愤怒农民长达八天的“行动周”，他们用拖拉机封锁了道路；铁路工人也举行了为期三天的罢工；更糟糕的是，医生们可能也要举行罢工，他们已经在圣诞节和元旦期间关闭了诊所。一些人称之为“干草叉暴民”（Mistgabelmop），这场风暴将在未来一年考验德国和谐的劳资关系。"
type: sentence
emotion: [serious, objective]
status: final
context: "Opening paragraph of a news article describing an unusual wave of strikes in Germany, including farmers, railway workers, and doctors. The tone is explanatory but vivid, with a German term introduced and glossed for the reader. Preceding segment: German farmers and train drivers are scaring Germany's bosses Following segment: The protests were ostensibly set off by the government's decision to end subsidies for di…"

<test-en-news-economist-14223-22>
source: "The protests were ostensibly set off by the government's decision to end subsidies for diesel fuel used in agriculture and to cut an exemption from car tax for farm vehicles. These measures pushed farmers over the edge. It also mobilised other angry workers, already straining under the pressure of inflation, recession and the government's self-imposed austerity. On January 9th drivers of freight and passenger trains at Deutsche Bahn, the national railway, began a strike over working hours and pay."
target: "表面上看，抗议活动的导火索是政府决定终止对农用柴油的补贴，并削减对农用车辆的汽车税豁免。这些措施让农民忍无可忍。这也带动了一些愤怒的工人，他们在通货膨胀、经济衰退和政府自我实施的紧缩政策的压力下苦苦挣扎。1 月 9 日，德国国家铁路公司的货运和客运列车司机就工作时间和工资问题举行罢工。"
type: sentence
emotion: [neutral, objective]
status: final
context: "News article passage explaining the causes of the German protests: the government's decision to end agricultural diesel subsidies and cut a car tax exemption. The tone is factual and analytical. Preceding segment: In Germany, where workers and bosses run many companies jointly, a big strike is unusual.… Following segment: In an effort to defuse the tension with the farmers, the government agreed to a gradual r…"

<test-en-news-economist-14223-23>
source: "In an effort to defuse the tension with the farmers, the government agreed to a gradual removal of the diesel subsidy over three years and to keeping the exemption from the car tax. The farmers pooh-poohed the concessions as insufficient. On January 4th an aggressive group of them prevented Robert Habeck, the economy minister, from disembarking from a ferry on his return from a family holiday. If the train drivers are similarly unimpressed, that could prove expensive for German business, reckons IW Köln, a think-tank. The rail strike could cost businesses €100m ($110m) a day if it forced them to interrupt production. The car, chemical and steel industries, Germany's biggest, are especially reliant on rail transport."
target: "为了缓和与农民之间的紧张关系，政府同意在三年内逐步取消柴油补贴，并保留汽车税的豁免政策。农民们对这些让步嗤之以鼻，认为远远不够。1 月 4 日，经济部长罗伯特·哈贝克在结束家庭假期后，乘坐渡轮返回时，遭到一群激进分子的阻拦，无法下船。智库 IW Köln 认为，如果火车司机也对政府的方案不买账，那么对德国企业来说，代价可能十分高昂。如果铁路罢工迫使企业中断生产，每天可能造成 1 亿欧元（1.1 亿美元）的损失。作为德国的支柱产业，汽车、化工和钢铁行业尤其依赖铁路运输。"
type: sentence
emotion: [serious, objective]
status: final
context: "News article passage describing the government's partial concessions to farmers, the farmers' rejection of them, and the potential economic cost of the rail strike. Includes a reference to a think-tank estimate. Preceding segment: The protests were ostensibly set off by the government's decision to end subsidies for di… Following segment: The workers\" mood is increasingly angry. \"Appeals are circulating with fantasies of revol…"

<test-en-news-economist-14223-24>
source: "The workers\" mood is increasingly angry. \"Appeals are circulating with fantasies of revolution,\" warned Mr Habeck. The far-right Alternative for Germany party is doing its best to fan the grievances. In Dresden the Free Saxons, another far-right group, infiltrated the farmers\" protest calling for the \"extinction of the traffic light\" (as the governing coalition of the Social Democrats, Free Democrats and Greens is referred to because of their party colours)."
target: "工人们的情绪越来越愤怒。“各种带有革命幻想的呼吁正在流传，”哈贝克先生警告说。极右翼政党德国选择党正在竭尽全力煽动不满情绪。在德累斯顿，另一个极右翼组织“自由撒克逊人”渗透到农民的抗议活动中，呼吁“熄灭交通灯”（由于其代表色，由社民党、自由民主党和绿党组成的执政联盟被称为“交通灯联盟”）。"
type: sentence
emotion: [anxious, serious]
status: final
context: "Closing passage of a news article about the increasingly angry mood among German workers, with a warning from the economy minister and mention of far-right groups exploiting the protests. The tone is cautionary. Preceding segment: In an effort to defuse the tension with the farmers, the government agreed to a gradual r… Following segment: Thomas Puls of IW Köln fears that the strikes will harm the image of Germany as a place f…"

<test-en-news-economist-14223-25>
source: "Thomas Puls of IW Köln fears that the strikes will harm the image of Germany as a place for business. Local bosses are already fretting about a German version of the gilets jaunes protests in France in 2018, which culminated in yellow-jacketed demonstrators torching cars on the Champs-Elysées and the police stepping in with tear gas. Jochen Kopelke, head of Germany's police union, warned in an interview with Tagesspiegel, a daily, that the farmers were probably \"just the start of an enormous wave of protest this year.\" Germany was the only big economy to shrink in 2023, and the year ended on an especially sour note, with an unexpected drop in business confidence in December. This year is shaping up to be even tougher."
target: "IW Köln 的托马斯·普尔斯担心，罢工将损害德国作为商业投资地的形象。当地老板们已经开始担心德国版“黄马甲”运动重演——2018 年的法国黄马甲运动最终演变成身穿黄马甲的示威者在香榭丽舍大街焚烧汽车，警察施放催泪瓦斯驱散人群。德国警察工会主席约亨·科佩尔克在接受《每日镜报》采访时警告说，农民的抗议活动可能“只是今年大规模抗议浪潮的开始”。2023 年，德国是唯一一个出现经济萎缩的主要经济体，年末经济形势尤其严峻，12 月商业信心指数意外下降。今年的经济形势预计将更加艰难。"
type: narration
emotion: [objective, serious]
status: final
